---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SubProjects from '@components/SubProjects.astro';
import Citation from '@components/Citation.astro';
---

<BaseLayout>
  <section class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-thmblue mb-4">
      The Theory of Persistence
    </h1>
    <p class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-sans font-semibold text-derorange mb-8">
      What persists is what remains under constraint.
    </p>

    <p data-max-depth="L1" class="text-lg text-stone-800 leading-relaxed mb-6 bg-amber-50 border-l-4 border-amber-300 px-4 py-3">
      <strong>In one sentence:</strong> what persists is not what remains by
      inertia, but what remains after admissible constraints. What dissipates
      becomes entropy; what persists becomes structure, then observable.
    </p>

    <p class="text-lg text-stone-800 leading-relaxed mb-6">
      The theory starts from an informational conservation law that is simple
      to say: when a system offers a certain number of possibilities, it has a
      total budget of distinctions. That budget splits exactly between two
      things: the part that remains structured, hence persistent, and the part
      that disperses, hence entropic. In compact notation, this becomes
      <span class="font-mono">log₂(m) = D_KL + H</span>. The sieve of
      Eratosthenes then enters as the minimal laboratory: it applies simple
      constraints, eliminates what does not survive, and reveals the
      persistence points where structure becomes computable.
    </p>

    <p class="text-lg text-stone-800 leading-relaxed mb-8">
      PT then tests this principle in three broad registers: mathematics,
      where persistence appears in survivors and gaps; physics, where it
      constrains constants, masses, geometry, and time; and chemistry, where it
      explains periods, shells, ionization energies, and electron affinities.
      Technical details remain available in L3 mode, but the natural entry is
      the idea: first understand what “persisting” means.
    </p>

    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 mb-12">
      <a
        href="/en/essays/idea-5min"
        class="px-5 py-3 bg-thmblue text-white font-sans font-semibold rounded hover:bg-thmblue/90"
      >
        The idea in 5 minutes
      </a>
      <a
        href="/en/commencer-ici"
        class="px-5 py-3 bg-white border border-thmblue text-thmblue font-sans font-semibold rounded hover:bg-thmblue/5"
      >
        Start here
      </a>
      <a
        href="/en/premier-principe"
        class="px-5 py-3 bg-white border border-thmblue text-thmblue font-sans font-semibold rounded hover:bg-thmblue/5"
      >
        Fundamental principle
      </a>
      <a
        href="/en/tableau-periodique"
        class="px-5 py-3 bg-white border border-thmblue text-thmblue font-sans font-semibold rounded hover:bg-thmblue/5"
      >
        First demonstration
      </a>
      <a
        href="/en/questions-fondamentales"
        class="px-5 py-3 bg-white border border-thmblue text-thmblue font-sans font-semibold rounded hover:bg-thmblue/5"
      >
        Fundamental questions
      </a>
      <a
        href="/en/predictions"
        class="px-5 py-3 bg-white border border-stone-300 text-stone-800 font-sans font-semibold rounded hover:bg-stone-50"
      >
        Predictions
      </a>
      <a
        href="/en/resultats"
        class="px-5 py-3 bg-white border border-stone-300 text-stone-800 font-sans font-semibold rounded hover:bg-stone-50"
      >
        Results dashboard
      </a>
      <a
        href="/en/observables"
        class="px-5 py-3 bg-white border border-stone-300 text-stone-800 font-sans font-semibold rounded hover:bg-stone-50"
      >
        43 observables
      </a>
      <a
        href="/en/temps"
        class="px-5 py-3 bg-white border border-stone-300 text-stone-800 font-sans font-semibold rounded hover:bg-stone-50"
      >
        Time
      </a>
      <a
        href="/en/relativite"
        class="px-5 py-3 bg-white border border-stone-300 text-stone-800 font-sans font-semibold rounded hover:bg-stone-50"
      >
        Relativity
      </a>
      <a
        href="/en/gravite-quantique"
        class="px-5 py-3 bg-white border border-stone-300 text-stone-800 font-sans font-semibold rounded hover:bg-stone-50"
      >
        Quantum gravity
      </a>
      <a
        href="/en/nucleaire"
        class="px-5 py-3 bg-white border border-stone-300 text-stone-800 font-sans font-semibold rounded hover:bg-stone-50"
      >
        Nuclear
      </a>
      <a
        href="/en/cosmologie"
        class="px-5 py-3 bg-white border border-stone-300 text-stone-800 font-sans font-semibold rounded hover:bg-stone-50"
      >
        Cosmology
      </a>
      <a
        href="/en/energies-ionisation"
        class="px-5 py-3 bg-white border border-stone-300 text-stone-800 font-sans font-semibold rounded hover:bg-stone-50"
      >
        Ionization energies
      </a>
      <a
        href="/en/affinites-electroniques"
        class="px-5 py-3 bg-white border border-stone-300 text-stone-800 font-sans font-semibold rounded hover:bg-stone-50"
      >
        Electron affinities
      </a>
      <a
        href="/en/preuve-interactive"
        class="px-5 py-3 bg-white border border-stone-300 text-stone-800 font-sans font-semibold rounded hover:bg-stone-50"
      >
        Interactive proof
      </a>
      <a
        href="/en/difficile-a-rejeter"
        class="px-5 py-3 bg-white border border-stone-300 text-stone-800 font-sans font-semibold rounded hover:bg-stone-50"
      >
        Hard to dismiss
      </a>
      <a
        href="/en/statuts-resultats"
        class="px-5 py-3 bg-white border border-stone-300 text-stone-800 font-sans font-semibold rounded hover:bg-stone-50"
      >
        Result status
      </a>
      <a
        href="/en/limites"
        class="px-5 py-3 bg-white border border-stone-300 text-stone-800 font-sans font-semibold rounded hover:bg-stone-50"
      >
        Limits
      </a>
      <a
        href="/en/theorems"
        class="px-5 py-3 bg-white border border-thmblue text-thmblue font-sans font-semibold rounded hover:bg-thmblue/5"
      >
        8 founding theorems
      </a>
      <a
        href="/en/monograph"
        class="px-5 py-3 bg-white border border-thmblue text-thmblue font-sans font-semibold rounded hover:bg-thmblue/5"
      >
        Read the monograph (EN 885 p. / FR 913 p.)
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-5 gap-4 text-sm mb-10">
      <a href="/en/theorems" class="pt-card block group">
        <span class="pt-tag pt-tag-thm">Mathematics</span>
        <h2 class="font-sans font-semibold text-thmblue mt-3 mb-2 group-hover:underline">
          The persistence points
        </h2>
        <p class="text-stone-700">
          The sieve serves as an exact laboratory: survivors, gaps, GFT, and
          theorems show how a constraint produces stable structures.
        </p>
      </a>
      <a href="/en/observables" class="pt-card block group">
        <span class="pt-tag pt-tag-der">Physics</span>
        <h2 class="font-sans font-semibold text-thmblue mt-3 mb-2 group-hover:underline">
          The principle tested
        </h2>
        <p class="text-stone-700">
          Couplings, masses, angles, time, and geometry: PT compares its
          persistent structures with physical measurements.
        </p>
      </a>
      <a href="/en/tableau-periodique" class="pt-card block group">
        <span class="pt-tag pt-tag-id">Chemistry</span>
        <h2 class="font-sans font-semibold text-thmblue mt-3 mb-2 group-hover:underline">
          Shell persistence
        </h2>
        <p class="text-stone-700">
          The sequence 2, 8, 8, 18, 18, 32, 32 becomes a consequence of
          persistent channels, spin doubling, and internal shells.
        </p>
      </a>
      <a href="/en/energies-ionisation" class="pt-card block group">
        <span class="pt-tag pt-tag-val">Chemistry</span>
        <h2 class="font-sans font-semibold text-thmblue mt-3 mb-2 group-hover:underline">
          Ionization energies
        </h2>
        <p class="text-stone-700">
          PT reconstructs peaks, closures, and relativistic residuals through a
          continuous reading of channels and radial depth.
        </p>
      </a>
      <a href="/en/affinites-electroniques" class="pt-card block group">
        <span class="pt-tag pt-tag-bridge">Chemistry</span>
        <h2 class="font-sans font-semibold text-thmblue mt-3 mb-2 group-hover:underline">
          Electron affinities
        </h2>
        <p class="text-stone-700">
          EA becomes a capture energy at the channel boundary, with a PT
          calculator, full table, and L1/L2/L3 reading.
        </p>
      </a>
    </div>

    <div data-min-depth="L3" class="bg-stone-50 border border-stone-300 rounded-lg p-4 my-6 text-sm">
      <p class="text-xs font-sans text-stone-500 uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">Technical note (L3 mode)</p>
      <p class="text-stone-700">
        The formal framework comprises base bridge axioms (BA0–BA2) that
        identify the dynamical field with the gaps between consecutive primes,
        then derived bridges (BA3–BA5) promoted or constrained in the chain,
        and a cascade of seven theorems (T0 → T6) deriving the holonomy angles
        sin²(θ_p) = δ_p(2 − δ_p) and the anomalous dimensions γ_p, and theorem
        T5 closing the fixed point μ* = 15 by exact rational exhaustion. The
        identity log₂(m) = D_KL(P‖U_m) + H(P) (GFT) is the
        <strong>fundamental principle of persistence</strong>: total informational
        capacity is conserved and partitions exactly into persistence and
        entropy.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 text-sm">
      <div class="pt-card">
        <span class="pt-tag pt-tag-thm">Theorems</span>
        <p class="mt-2 text-stone-700">
          T0 → T6, GFT, L0 — complete chain, zero drift across versions.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="pt-card">
        <span class="pt-tag pt-tag-der">Derivations</span>
        <p class="mt-2 text-stone-700">
          43 observables, mean error 0.30%, median 0.06%, zero fit.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="pt-card">
        <span class="pt-tag pt-tag-val">Verification</span>
        <p class="mt-2 text-stone-700">
          Canonical registry: 45 companion script entries, 2,522/2,523 passing checks — flagship scripts runnable in the browser.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <SubProjects lang="en" />

    <Citation lang="en" />

    <p class="mt-12 text-sm text-stone-500 italic font-sans">
      Preprint — not peer-reviewed. Critical scrutiny is welcomed.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
